ew, monospace\">4     1  2005<br></font><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">5     1  2006<br></font><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">6     1  2007</font></blockquote></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div>but translating this to <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">dplyr</font> eludes me. both of these fail:</div><div><br></div><div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">tbl_df(d1) %&gt;%</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    group_by(indiv) %&gt;%</font></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\">    data.frame(years = seq(start, end, 1))</font></div></div><div><font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><br></font></div><div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">tbl_df(d1) %&gt;%</div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">    group_by(indiv) %&gt;%</div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\">    summarize(years = seq(start, end, 1))</div><div style=\"font-family:&#39;courier new&#39;,monospace\"><br></div><div>how can you do this in dplyr?</div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>This works:</div><div><br></div><div>   d1 %&gt;% group_by(indiv) %&gt;% do(data.frame(year = .$start:.$end)) <br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
